WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:02.676
- Don't be an asshole, period.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.152
And that pretty much covers it,

00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:06.965
and also, you can go right
into the Golden Rule,

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.888
treat people like you wanna be treated.

00:00:08.888 --> 00:00:11.768
(cheerful music)

00:00:11.768 --> 00:00:12.864
- [Voiceover] Well hey there.

00:00:12.864 --> 00:00:14.696
Look, it's Willie.

00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:15.788
- [Voiceover] In the 1930s,

00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:17.948
Willie Nelson was a small-town kid.

00:00:17.948 --> 00:00:20.636
He was also an extreme nose-picker.

00:00:20.636 --> 00:00:21.836
He'd pick until he bled,

00:00:21.836 --> 00:00:24.427
and Willie became an
easy target for bullies.

00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:25.893
(laughter)

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:27.760
- When I was like six years old,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.024
my grandmother had taught
me this poem, said,

00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:31.344
what are you looking at me for?

00:00:31.344 --> 00:00:33.544
I ain't got nothing to say.

00:00:33.544 --> 00:00:35.364
If you don't like the looks of me,

00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:38.064
you can just look the other way.

00:00:38.064 --> 00:00:39.384
And I thought it was so funny,

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:42.471
I started living that way (laughs).

00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:44.032
- [Voiceover] He learned
to ignore the teasing

00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:45.864
and look the other way.

00:00:45.864 --> 00:00:48.908
And years later, that lesson still stands.

00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:50.740
- Well, I think you have
to follow your feelings,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.073
do what your conscience tells you to do.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.396
If you feel like you can do anything,

00:00:57.396 --> 00:01:00.771
whether it's this cause or that cause,

00:01:00.771 --> 00:01:03.220
I think you're obligated to do it.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.884
- [Voiceover] For Willie,
offering a helping hand

00:01:04.884 --> 00:01:06.620
has played an important role.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.260
He's supported dozens of environmental

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.812
and humanitarian causes over the years.

00:01:11.812 --> 00:01:14.180
- I feel like we're all
responsible for each other, you know.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.588
If you see somebody
out need some help,

00:01:17.588 --> 00:01:19.944
you help 'em, if you see
somebody's cow in a ditch,

00:01:19.944 --> 00:01:22.312
you help 'em pull ‘er out.

00:01:22.312 --> 00:01:23.164
(cow lowing)

00:01:23.164 --> 00:01:24.592
(laughter)

00:01:24.592 --> 00:01:27.621
I like to think that we all gotta be

00:01:27.621 --> 00:01:30.538
as good an example as we can be,

00:01:31.408 --> 00:01:35.587
whether it's to our kids
or to the whole world.

00:01:35.587 --> 00:01:38.337
(cheerful music)

